    "en": "Indirect questions",
    "es": "Preguntas indirectas",
    "it": "Domande indirette",
    "fr": "Questions indirectes",
    "de": "Indirekte Fragen",
    "ru": "Косвенные вопросы",
    "hu": "Függő kérdések",
    "pt": "Perguntas indiretas",
    "ro": "Întrebări indirecte"
  },
  "locales": {
    "en": {
      "title": "Indirect questions",
      "summary": "An indirect question keeps statement word order.",
      "status": "draft",
      "sections": [
        {
          "title": "What it is",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraphs",
              "paragraphs": [
                "An indirect question is a question inside another sentence. It sounds more polite."
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Do you know **where he lives**?",
                "I wonder **what time it is**.",
                "Can you tell me **how much it costs**?"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "How it works in English",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraphs",
              "paragraphs": [
                "In an indirect question the word order is the same as in a statement: no inversion and no do. If there is no question word, use if or whether."
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "html": "<table><thead><tr><th>Direct</th><th>Indirect</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Where is the bank?</strong></td><td><strong>Do you know where the bank is?</strong></td></tr><tr><td><strong>Does he know?</strong></td><td><strong>I wonder if he knows.</strong></td></tr></tbody></table>"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  }
}
